BUILD-OUTPUT: bind the embedded ICC profile to the render that produced it

The delivered SHIP-V2 gallery was measured first, on real bytes, with a
from-scratch IFD walker (tifffile normalises a missing resolution to 1/1 and so
cannot tell absent from present-and-default). All 26 masters carry NO ICC
profile (34675 absent) and ResolutionUnit = 1 (none). The code at HEAD is
already correct on all three colour modes -- 96b7e119 landed ICC, c14284a8
landed resolution -- and the gallery simply predates both by hours. Routed to
ORCH: the artifacts are stale, the writer is not.

What the ICC tests could not see, each verified by planting the defect and
watching the suite stay green:

  * only_the_colorimetric_paths_get_a_profile ends with assert_ne!(srgb, lin).
    An inequality fixes no identity: exchange the two arms of icc_for and every
    assertion in the crate still passes while --srgb files carry the linear
    profile. Prior lanes measured that swap at 50.39 DN mean over 99.5% of
    pixels (BUILD-RENDER-icc/potency.py) and 92 DN (icc_potency.py ARM B).
  * OutputSpace::Srgb.develop(None) was never covered -- an uncharacterised
    body rendered --srgb, camera primaries carrying an sRGB curve, the mode
    that looks most like sRGB and is least like it.
  * icc_for matched on (matrix, srgb) only, so a development with the matrix
    and a tone but no transfer curve -- s_curve applied in linear light -- fell
    into the linear arm and got a profile describing something else.

icc_for is now a total match on (matrix, srgb, tone), the third state
answering None: the same wrong-profile-is-worse-than-none policy the
camera-native paths already followed, applied one step further in.

the_embedded_profile_states_the_transfer_curve_the_pixels_carry is new and is
deliberately file-level: it writes a TIFF per mode, reads tag 34675 back out,
and walks the ICC tag table as raw bytes rather than through a parser shared
with the writer, which would agree with the writer by construction. It asserts
the TRC is identity iff no curve was applied and sampled-sRGB (TRC(0.5) =
0.2140, not 0.735) iff it was, that gTRC/bTRC alias rTRC, that the desc string
and the curve agree, that the colorants match srgb_to_xyz_d50(), and that the
tag is absent on the three modes nothing here can describe.

Commissioned in experiments/BUILD-OUTPUT/commission_icc.ps1, four arms:

  CLEAN     -> new test OK,     30 passed
  SWAP      -> new test FAILED, all five pre-existing ICC tests ok
  THIRDARM  -> new test FAILED, all five pre-existing ICC tests ok
  BACKWARDS -> new test FAILED, all five pre-existing ICC tests ok

On all three planted defects every pre-existing ICC test stayed green, so the
new test is the only thing in the crate with power over any of them. THIRDARM
reverts the improvement this commit makes and reads RED, which is the planted-
improvement direction rule 2 requires. BACKWARDS turned up an unplanned
finding: the_transfer_curve_is_stored_in_the_decoding_direction tests the
helper srgb_eotf, not what lands in the file, and stays green when the inverse
is inlined at the call site.

Highlights and shadows, measured rather than argued (docs/research):

  * dry-erase-marker-head-cpl's 0.3265% clip was real and is already fixed at
    HEAD by the highlight roll-off: pin b9b6921e 0.6109%, HEAD with
    STREHL_HIGHLIGHT_KNEE=off 0.6109% (four decimals), HEAD default 0.0000%.
    Under alignment, 0.3265% -> 0.0000%. Its clipALL3 was 0.0000%, the corpus
    minimum -- the gate failed the one master with zero blown highlights.
  * flowers-cpl is not a highlight failure. clipALL3 0.0131%, while sixteen
    subjects that PASSED have more, up to 112MSDCF at 0.0693%. A single source
    frame carries 90% of it, --exposure 1.76 and --auto-exposure (+1.91) give
    bit-identical statistics, and knees of 0.60/0.45/0.30 are bit-identical --
    the roll-off works in camera space and cannot reach it. Recorded in
    DEFAULT_KNEE's doc comment so the sweep is not re-run.
  * All three crush subjects are innocent. crushALL3 is 0.0000% for 25 of 26
    masters; the flagged pixels have median luminance 0.24-0.33 with 33k-53k
    distinct surviving levels, against 0.0011 and 122 levels for flowers-cpl's
    genuine black. The statistic is anti-correlated with the property it names
    and must not earn an absolute threshold.

Verified: strehl-core 510 passed / 0 failed; strehl-cli 110 passed / 0 failed;
byte-freeze 5 passed, both rows HOLD at their recorded hashes, reproduced
twice. The byte-freeze was checked rather than assumed -- both rows render
camera-native through the untagged write_rgb16, but "should not move" is not a
measurement.
